                <pb facs="0365" n="285" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg285"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Hart</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-02-20"><hi rendition="#italic">February 20,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay directs Mr. Hart to demand of the Colombian Government immediate
                    restitution of the vessels of the Fluvial Company of Cartagena, and full
                    indemnity for damages occasioned by their seizure and use; and also to demand
                    full indemnity for use of and damages done to the Cartagena-Magdalena Railway
                    Company.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
